  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output A.1. More accurate and sustainable statistics on decent work using the latest statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">During this biennium, the Central Administration of Statistics in Lebanon conducted a follow-up survey providing updated key data and statistics on the post-crises labour market situation in Lebanon.

The Central Administration of Statistics (CAS) in Lebanon has adopted an improved Labour Force Survey (LFS) questionnaire, following the latest statistical standards and methods adopted by the 20th International Conference of Labour Statisticians (ICLS). The ILO supported the development of the questionnaire and all data collection- related preparatory work.
The ILO provided technical support in questionnaire design and questionnaire testing. 

The ILO provided capacity building and technical support to staff of CAS via the organization of two IT trainings for the implementation of the CsPro. Four staff benefitted from the trainings.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">A.1.1. Number of member States that strengthen their labour market statistics, standards and information systems through improved statistical surveys and use of other statistical sources</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Strengthened social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Association of Lebanese Industrialists (ALI) and the General Confederation of Lebanese Workers (CGTL) agreed to enhance health and safety measures at workplace level through enhanced bipartite dialogue, and decided on focal points to select priority sectors, share the existing guidelines and protocols, and develop a joint communication strategy.

ALI and CGTL agreed to increase transportation allowance for workers in the private sector in light of the economic crisis and currency depreciation in Lebanon. With RBSA funding, the ILO provided technical support to ALI and CGTL leaders to hold their first meeting on May 31, 2021, where they agreed to develop joint national guidelines for safe and healthful working conditions during pandemic outbreak times in Lebanon.

In October-November 2021, the ILO, following consultations with social partners, delivered a report including mapping of all the guidelines and protocols issued by Lebanese authorities or sectoral organizations and recommendations for workplace level prevention measures based on best practices. 

In December 2021: the ILO facilitated a bipartite workshop (virtual) to share the results of the mapping and recommendations for implementation of the guidelines. At the end of the workshop there was a specific request to transform the recommendations for better workplace prevention into a 4-pager factsheet to be distributed to companies and trade unions via a communication campaign.</narrative>
   </description>
